From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:37:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: back navigation: add kde_back_navigation_v1 and its shell protocol
Description:
 kde_back_navigation_v1 lets a client report per xdg_toplevel whether back
 currently has an effect in it and delivers a back event to the toplevel.
 kde_back_navigation_shell_v1 gives a client that holds an
 org_kde_plasma_window access to that state and lets it ask for back in that
 window, so a shell can offer one back control for all applications, for
 example in the navigation bar of a phone.
 .
 The state is kept per Window (Window::isBackAvailable()) and passed on to
 PlasmaWindowInterface. A back request reaches the client only while the
 state is available and the window can take input: not while a modal dialog
 blocks it and not while the session is locked, unless the window is shown
 above the lock screen.
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-2.0-or-later and LGPL-2.1-only OR LGPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL (as the patched files; new files under src/wayland/ LGPL-2.1-only OR LGPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL, protocol XML files MIT)
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
